## 18. Termination and cure

Except for breaches subject to immediate termination below, if you materially breach this License and the breach is reasonably capable of correction, ITECOB will provide notice of the breach and you will have 30 days after receiving notice to fully cure it.

If you fully cure the breach within that 30-day period, your rights under this License will continue and will not terminate because of that cured breach. If you do not fully cure it within that period, your rights under this License terminate at the end of the cure period.

ITECOB may terminate rights immediately, to the extent permitted by law, where the breach involves:

- deliberate or repeated violation of the commercial-use restrictions;
- unlawful use;
- intentional false claims of ITECOB affiliation, certification, verification, approval, or endorsement;
- deliberate removal or falsification of required licence, attribution, provenance, or modification notices; or
- conduct that cannot reasonably be cured.

Termination does not retroactively make previously compliant conduct unlawful and does not remove obligations, liabilities, or restrictions that by their nature survive termination.

goodLAC contains no technical licence-enforcement, telemetry, remote-monitoring, or phone-home mechanism for the purpose of detecting licence violations. Compliance remains the licensee's responsibility. ITECOB may enforce this License when it becomes aware of sufficient evidence of a breach through lawful means.

